.TH QFW-SERVICES.YAML 5 "August 2026" "QFw 0.1.0" "QFw File Formats"
.SH NAME
qfw-services.yaml \- define QPM service implementations and placement
.SH DESCRIPTION
A QFw service manifest is YAML containing a
.B services
sequence. Each entry names one QPM service and describes the DEFw module,
placement, provider launcher, and optional device identity.
.SH MPI LAUNCH KEYS
An optional top-level
.B mpi-launch
mapping sets how MPI providers run
.BR mpirun .
The installed local manifest sets no transport or placement. A site that needs
them names its own manifest through
.B service-manifest
in
.BR qfw-runtime.yaml (5).
.TP
.B launcher
The MPI launcher. The default is
.BR mpirun .
.TP
.B allow-run-as-root
.BR auto ,
.BR true ,
or
.BR false .
.TP
.B export-env
Environment variables passed with
.BR -x .
.TP
.B mca
A mapping of MCA parameters passed with
.BR --mca .
These take precedence over
.B OMPI_MCA_*
variables.
.TP
.BR map-by ", " bind-to
Passed as
.B --map-by
and
.BR --bind-to .
.TP
.B extra-args
A list added to every command.
.SH SERVICE KEYS
.TP
.B name
Manifest selector for the QPM implementation. A site-owned QPM also uses this
as its stable service ID. QFw combines this name with the application run ID
to create a unique service ID for an application-owned QPM.
.TP
.B module
Primary DEFw QPM module.
.TP
.B load-modules
Comma-separated DEFw module load list. It normally includes the QPM module and
.BR api_launcher .
.TP
.B environment-modules
YAML sequence of site environment modules loaded before an optional PRTE DVM
and the QPM start. This is separate from
.BR load-modules ,
which names Python modules loaded by DEFw. A missing module is a startup error.
.TP
.B required-executables
YAML sequence of executable names that must be available after environment
module loading. QFw validates them before starting PRTE or the QPM.
.TP
.B agent-prefix
Prefix used for QPM agents created by the service.
.TP
.B host
Host used for a site-scoped service.
.TP
.B target
Application-scope placement policy. Common values are
.BR group1-head ,
.BR group0-head ,
and
.BR local .
.TP
.B assigned-hosts
Host assignment policy passed to the QPM. Common values are
.BR group1 ,
.BR group0 ,
and
.BR all .
.TP
.B assigned-hosts-env
Additional environment variable that receives the resolved host list.
.TP
.B listen-port
DEFw service listen port.
.TP
.B telnet-port
DEFw diagnostic telnet port.
.TP
.B device-id
Device identifier resolved through the protected configuration described by
.BR qfw-device-access.yaml (5).
.TP
.B provider-launch
Provider execution mapping. The
.B type
key commonly selects
.BR internal ,
.BR mpi ,
.BR remote-api ,
or
.BR qrmi-qdmi .
Provider-specific keys may include
.B wrapper
and
.BR use-dvm .
.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
services:
  - name: nwqsim
    module: svc_nwqsim_qpm
    load-modules: svc_nwqsim_qpm,api_launcher
    environment-modules:
      - libfabric
      - nwqsim
    required-executables:
      - circuit_runner.nwqsim
    agent-prefix: qpm_nwqsim
    provider-launch:
      type: mpi
      use-dvm: true
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qfw-qpm-svc (1),
.BR qfw-service-lifecycle (7),
.BR qfw-device-access.yaml (5),
.BR qfw-runtime.yaml (5),
.BR qfw-site.yaml (5)
